1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,455
What if the ocean stopped moving for one minute?

2
00:00:03,495 --> 00:00:04,874
Waves are rolling in,

3
00:00:04,914 --> 00:00:06,902
gulls are screaming, and then,

4
00:00:06,942 --> 00:00:08,659
in the middle of a splash,

5
00:00:08,699 --> 00:00:09,944
every drop freezes.

6
00:00:09,984 --> 00:00:12,242
The whole sea goes still as glass.

7
00:00:13,650 --> 00:00:15,699
People creep toward the shore.

8
00:00:15,739 --> 00:00:18,484
A surfer hangs in a perfect barrel wave,

9
00:00:18,524 --> 00:00:20,643
frozen mid-ride, still smiling.

10
00:00:20,683 --> 00:00:22,035
Kids poke the water,

11
00:00:22,075 --> 00:00:23,567
and it doesn't ripple.

12
00:00:23,607 --> 00:00:24,890
It just sits there,

13
00:00:24,930 --> 00:00:26,561
like a giant blue jelly.

14
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:28,742
Then someone has an idea.

15
00:00:28,782 --> 00:00:31,651
They stand directly in front of the frozen

16
00:00:31,691 --> 00:00:33,245
wave and take a selfie.

17
00:00:33,285 --> 00:00:36,085
Soon, the beach is crowded with tourists,

18
00:00:36,125 --> 00:00:38,648
all grinning in front of a giant blue

19
00:00:38,688 --> 00:00:39,618
wall of water.

20
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:43,928
At forty seconds, a scientist runs onto the

21
00:00:43,968 --> 00:00:45,435
beach, waving her arms.

22
00:00:45,475 --> 00:00:46,942
If this wave unfreezes,

23
00:00:46,982 --> 00:00:49,629
she shouts, we need to be somewhere else.

24
00:00:49,669 --> 00:00:52,971
Everyone suddenly remembers what waves actually do.

25
00:00:53,450 --> 00:00:55,022
So the whole town runs uphill,

26
00:00:55,062 --> 00:00:58,731
carrying umbrellas, sandwiches, and one extremely confused dachshund.

27
00:00:58,771 --> 00:01:00,397
Meanwhile, the countdown ticks.

28
00:01:00,437 --> 00:01:03,460
Hypothetically, the ocean has never been so well-behaved.

29
00:01:03,850 --> 00:01:04,931
In a real world,

30
00:01:04,971 --> 00:01:06,262
oceans can't pause.

31
00:01:06,302 --> 00:01:08,575
They carry far too much momentum,

32
00:01:08,615 --> 00:01:11,167
so this is only a thought experiment.

33
00:01:11,207 --> 00:01:12,779
But picture every tide,

34
00:01:12,819 --> 00:01:16,773
every current, and every wave holding its breath at once.

35
00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:18,417
Here's the twist.

36
00:01:18,457 --> 00:01:20,974
At the very center of the stillness,

37
00:01:21,014 --> 00:01:24,667
a huge whale rises and sings one long, glowing note.

38
00:01:24,707 --> 00:01:26,371
The ocean wasn't frozen.

39
00:01:26,411 --> 00:01:28,218
It was stopping to listen.

40
00:01:28,750 --> 00:01:30,035
Ten, nine, eight...

41
00:01:30,075 --> 00:01:31,151
The minute ends.

42
00:01:31,191 --> 00:01:33,522
The wave tumbles gently into foam,

43
00:01:33,562 --> 00:01:35,963
the sea sighs, and everyone cheers.

44
00:01:36,003 --> 00:01:38,334
A single whale tail waves goodbye,

45
00:01:38,374 --> 00:01:41,263
and the ocean goes back to its usual song.
